If the evaluator succeeds at the pair of an index and a certificate, then the catamorphism relates the sharp neighbourhood of that index to the neighbourhood coded by the certificate's output component, assuming the guard functions decide equality with the master and the relations of the two algebra maps.

A strengthening, in which the combined code equals the induction parameter, is proved by strong induction. At zero, the master clause and the decision property of the master guard give the master clause of the relation. At an odd code, the leaf clause and the decision property of the leaf guard give the leaf clause. At an even code, the node clause reads the two children from the memo table. Their codes are strictly smaller by mixed monotonicity of pairing and the bounds on the decoded certificate components, so the inductive hypothesis supplies their relations. The output components of those evaluations are the output components of the child certificates, and the decision property of the node guard supplies the node clause.
